  "featureGroup": false,
  "description": "The \u0027commits_cached\u0027 dataset provides detailed information about software project commits, capturing essential data for version control analysis. Each entry in the dataset represents a unique commit within a software project, identified by a \u0027project_key\u0027 and \u0027commit_id\u0027. The dataset includes the \u0027author\u0027 of the commit, allowing for tracking contributions by different developers. The \u0027timestamp\u0027 column records the exact time of the commit, facilitating chronological analysis of project development. Additionally, the dataset tracks changes made in each commit, including the number of \u0027added_files\u0027, \u0027added_lines\u0027, \u0027removed_files\u0027, \u0027removed_lines\u0027, and \u0027changed_files\u0027. This information is crucial for understanding the impact of each commit on the project\u0027s codebase, enabling insights into development patterns, code churn, and the overall evolution of the software. The dataset is particularly useful for software development teams, project managers, and researchers interested in software engineering metrics, providing a comprehensive view of code changes over time.",
  "shortDesc": "Software project commit data with author, timestamp, and file changes.",
